From 022a7ebae5f24ff50e14756a9eaff098324949f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: platform <platform@system.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 03:24:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mm: a "Source" link on every page of the gateway side (AGPL
 section 13)

People use this Doop over the network through mm's sign-in gateway, so
the gateway side offers them the source of the version they run: every
HTML page it serves gets a small "Source" link, just before </body>, to
DOOP_SOURCE_URL (the fork's source at the tag the image is built from,
DOOP_SOURCE_TAG; mm sets both from its pin). The page is not compressed
for that, asked in full (no 304 of a page without the link), sent without
ETag/Last-Modified, and a Content-Security-Policy gets the link's style
hash where it would refuse it.

Without a URL (or with one that is not http(s), or has credentials), the
link goes to /.mm-source/<tag> on the gateway side: a page that names the
tag, the upstream version and mm's patches. Doop's own listener (PORT) is
unchanged.
